# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its system config, so a default
# Windows clone checks text files out as CRLF while the index stays LF. Prettier
# only ever writes LF, so without normalising here `prettier --check` fails on
# every file locally while passing in CI (which checks out LF) — making the
# local format check useless. Keep the working tree LF on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
